messages:
Anya W: Customer report - Next.js edge sample fails at runtime; Node build is fine. Error: "TypeError: client.create is not a function". Seems related to ESM/CJS interop plus some TS overloads/generics weirdness. Anyone seen this crop up after swc/rollup builds?

Matt R: Yep. Bundlers sometimes rewrite exports and introduce a default shim. If a consumer ends up calling the shimmed export it can be a different value at runtime. Do we have a minimal repro?

Anya W: Pasted minimal repro below. TSC passes locally. Edge bundle throws.

```ts
// sdk/api.ts
export function createClient<T>(opts: { auth: string }): Client<T>;
export function createClient(opts: { auth?: string }): Client<any> {
  return new Client(opts.auth);
}

// consumer.ts
const client = createClient<{ user: { id: string } }>({ auth: process.env.TOK });
client.create({ user: { id: '123' } });
```

Jordan P: Classic. Overload + erased generics can cause TypeScript to pick the non-generic overload during compilation, while at runtime the exported function shape changes after bundling. The inference fallback to any vs unknown can bite you.

Sasha L: Actionable fixes: (1) SDK exports - prefer a single named ESM entry for edge builds (no dual require/import shims). (2) TS surface - avoid multiple overloads for createClient; use a single generic signature with a default or helper narrowers so inference survives bundling.

Matt R: Also check package.json "exports" map. For edge we should point to an ESM-only dist path, e.g. "./dist/edge/index.mjs" under "exports" for the edge subpath. That reduces bundler ambiguity.

Jordan P: Small code workaround: collapse overloads into one generic implementation so inference is stable. Example shorthand: 
```ts
export function createClient<T = any>(opts: { auth?: string } & { _marker?: T }) {
  // impl
}
```
For callers, forcing the generic explicitly works too: createClient<MyType>({}). Not ideal but effective.

Anya W: Also noticed our auth/refresh retry logic failed on edge because the fetch polyfill drops keepalive and timing differs. The sample's retry loop ended up aborting. We should document edge differences and provide an edge-friendly retry helper.

Sasha L: Agreed. Recommend using AbortController with shorter timeouts and idempotency guards on edge. I'll add a note in the samples and docs.

Anya W: Agreed action items: Matt - add ESM-only edge export and sanity-check exports map; Jordan - PR to reduce overload surface or add explicit generic guidance; Sasha - update sample tsconfig + docs about edge fetch/auth/retry.

Matt R: Starting a canary for the sample changes. tagging deploy-bot. :rocket:

deploy-bot: Canary deploy started for sample-app-edge (canary-1793456800). Logs: https://deploys.internal/sample-app-edge/canary-1793456800

Anya W: Thanks. If error persists paste compiled bundle export snippet so we can inspect interop shim.

Jordan P: Also adding a CI smoke test: quick esbuild + run in a Node edge-like environment to catch export-shim regressions early.

Sasha L: Filing docs PR now.

Anya W: Closing loop once canary proves green. :thumbsup:
